#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:3
msgid "Log/Log10/Log2 Algorithm"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:5
msgid ""
"In this short note, we will discuss in detail about the computation of {math}"
"`\\log(x)` function, with double precision inputs, in particular, the range "
"reduction steps and error analysis. The algorithm is broken down into 2 main "
"phases as follow:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:10
msgid "Fast phase:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:12 ../../../headers/math/log.md:23
msgid "Range reduction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:13 ../../../headers/math/log.md:19
msgid "Polynomial approximation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:14
msgid "Ziv's test"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:16
msgid "Accurate phase (if Ziv's test failed):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:18
msgid "Further range reduction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:21
msgid "Fast phase"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:25
msgid ""
"Let {math}`x = 2^{e_x} (1 + m_x)` be a normalized double precision number, "
"in which {math}`-1074 \\leq e_x \\leq 1022` and {math}`0 \\leq m_x < 1` such "
"that {math}`2^{52} m_x \\in \\mathbb{Z}`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:29
msgid "Then from the properties of logarithm:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:31
msgid ""
"\\log(x) &= \\log\\left( 2^{e_x} (1 + m_x) \\right) \\\\\n"
"        &= \\log\\left( 2^{e_x} \\right) + \\log(1 + m_x) \\\\\n"
"        &= e_x \\log(2) + \\log(1 + m_x)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:37
msgid "the computation of {math}`\\log(x)` can be reduced to:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:39
msgid "compute the product of {math}`e_x` and {math}`\\log(2)`,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:40
msgid "compute {math}`\\log(1 + m_x)` for {math}`0 \\leq m_x < 1`,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:41
msgid "add step 1 and 2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:43
msgid ""
"To compute {math}`\\log(1 + m_x)` in step 2, we can reduce the range further "
"by finding {math}`r > 0` such that:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:46
msgid "| r(1 + m_x) - 1 | < C \\quad \\quad \\text{(R1)}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:50
msgid ""
"for small {math}`0 < C < 1`. Then if we let {math}`u = r(1 + m_x) - 1`, "
"{math}`|u| < C`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:52
msgid ""
"\\log(1 + m_x) &= \\log \\left( \\frac{r (1 + m_x)}{r} \\right) \\\\\n"
"              &= \\log(r (1 + m_x) ) - \\log(r) \\\\\n"
"              &= \\log(1 + u) - \\log(r)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:58
msgid "and step 2 can be computed with:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:60
msgid "extract {math}`r` and {math}`-\\log(r)` from look-up tables,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:61
msgid "compute the reduced argument {math}`u = r(1 + m_x) - 1`,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:62
msgid ""
"compute {math}`\\log(1 + u)` by polynomial approximation or further range "
"reduction,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:63
msgid "add the results of items 1 and 3."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:65
msgid "How to derive {math}`r`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:67
msgid ""
"For an efficient implementation, we would like to use the first {math}`M` "
"significant bits of {math}`m_x` to look up for {math}`r`. In particular, we "
"would like to find a value of {math}`r` that works for all {math}`m_x` "
"satisfying:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:71
msgid ""
"k 2^{-M} \\leq m_x < (k + 1) 2^{-M} \\quad \\text{for some} \\quad\n"
"k = 0..2^{M} - 1. \\quad\\quad \\text{(M1)}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:76
msgid ""
"Let {math}`r = 1 + s`, then {math}`u` can be expressed in terms of {math}`s` "
"as:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:78
msgid ""
"u &= r(1 + m_x) - 1 \\\\\n"
"  &= (1 + s)(1 + m_x) - 1 \\\\\n"
"  &= s m_x + s + m_x  &\\quad\\quad \\text{(U1)} \\\\\n"
"  &= s (1 + m_x) + m_x \\\\\n"
"  &= m_x (1 + s) + s."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:86
msgid "From the condition {math}`\\text{(R1)}`, {math}`s` is bounded by:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:88
msgid ""
"\\frac{-C - m_x}{1 + m_x} < s < \\frac{C - m_x}{1 + m_x} \\quad\\quad "
"\\text{(S1)}."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:92
msgid ""
"Since our reduction constant {math}`s` must work for all {math}`m_x` in the "
"interval {math}`I = \\{ v: k 2^{-M} \\leq v < (k + 1) 2^{-M} \\}`, {math}`s` "
"is bounded by:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:95
msgid ""
"\\sup_{v \\in I} \\frac{-C - v}{1 + v} < s < \\inf_{v \\in I} \\frac{C - v}"
"{1 + v}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:99
msgid ""
"For a fixed constant {math}`|c| < 1`, let {math}`f(v) = \\frac{c - v}{1 + v}"
"`, then its derivative is:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:102
msgid ""
"f'(v) = \\frac{(-1)(1 + v) - (1)(c - v)}{(1 + v)^2} = \\frac{-1 - c}{(1 + "
"v)^2}."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:106
msgid ""
"Since {math}`|c| < 1`, {math}`f'(v) < 0` for all {math}`v \\neq -1`, so:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:108
msgid ""
"\\sup_{v \\in I} f(v) &= f \\left( \\inf\\{ v: v \\in I \\} \\right)\n"
"                     = f \\left( k 2^{-M} \\right) \\\\\n"
"\\inf_{v \\in I} f(v) &= f \\left( \\sup\\{ v: v \\in I \\} \\right)\n"
"                     = f \\left( (k + 1) 2^{-M} \\right)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:115
msgid "Hence we have the following bound on {math}`s`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:117
msgid ""
"\\frac{-C - k 2^{-M}}{1 + k 2^{-M}} < s \\leq\n"
"\\frac{C - (k + 1) 2^{-M}}{1 + (k + 1) 2^{-M}}. \\quad\\quad \\text{(S2)}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:122
msgid "In order for {math}`s` to exist, we need that:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:124
msgid ""
"\\frac{C - (k + 1) 2^{-M}}{1 + (k + 1) 2^{-M}} >\n"
"\\frac{-C - k 2^{-M}}{1 + k 2^{-M}}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:129
msgid "which is equivalent to:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:131
msgid ""
"\\quad\\quad 2C - 2^{-M} + (2k + 1) 2^{-M} C > 0\n"
"\\iff C > \\frac{2^{-M - 1}}{1 + (2k + 1) 2^{-M - 1}} \\quad\\quad "
"\\text{(C1)}."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:136
msgid ""
"Consider the case {math}`C = 2^{-N}`. Since {math}`0 \\leq k \\leq 2^M - 1,` "
"the right hand side of {math}`\\text{(C1)}` is bounded by:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:139
msgid ""
"2^{-M - 1} > \\frac{2^{-M - 1}}{1 + (2k + 1) 2^{-M - 1}} \\geq\n"
"\\frac{2^{-M - 1}}{1 + (2^{M + 1} - 1) 2^{-M - 1}} > 2^{-M - 2}."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:144
msgid ""
"Hence, from {math}`\\text{(C1)}`, being an exact power of 2, {math}`C = 2^{-"
"N}` is bounded below by:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:147
msgid "C = 2^{-N} \\geq 2^{-M - 1}."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:151
msgid ""
"To make the range reduction efficient, we will want to minimize {math}`C` "
"(maximize {math}`N`) while keeping the required precision of {math}`s`({math}"
"`r`) as low as possible. And for that, we will consider the following two "
"cases: {math}`N = M + 1` and {math}`N = M`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:155
msgid "Case 1 - {math}`N = M + 1`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:157
msgid "When {math}`N = M + 1`, {math}`\\text{(S2)}` becomes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:159
msgid ""
"\\frac{-2^{-M - 1} - k 2^{-M}}{1 + k 2^{-M}} < s <\n"
"\\frac{2^{-M - 1} - (k + 1) 2^{-M}}{1 + (k + 1) 2^{-M}}.\n"
"\\quad\\quad \\text{(S2')}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:165 ../../../headers/math/log.md:265
msgid "This is an interval of length:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:167
msgid ""
"l &= \\frac{2^{-M - 1} - (k + 1) 2^{-M}}{1 + (k + 1) 2^{-M}} -\n"
"     \\frac{-2^{-M - 1} - k 2^{-M}}{1 + k 2^{-M}} \\\\\n"
"  &= \\frac{(2k + 1)2^{-2M - 1}}{(1 + k 2^{-M})(1 + (k + 1)2^{-M})}\n"
"  \\quad\\quad \\text{(L1)}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:174
msgid ""
"As a function of {math}`k`, the length {math}`l` has its derivative with "
"respect to {math}`k`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:176
msgid ""
"\\frac{dl}{dk} =\n"
"\\frac{2^{2M + 1} - 2k(k + 1) - 1}\n"
"     {2^{4M}(1 + k 2^{-M})^2 (1 + (k + 1) 2^{-M})^2}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:182
msgid ""
"which is always positive for {math}`0 \\leq k \\leq 2^M - 1`. So for all "
"{math}`0 < k < 2^{-M}` ({math}`k = 0` will be treated differently in edge "
"cases), and for {math}`M > 2`, {math}`l` is bounded below by:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:186
msgid "l > 2^{-2M}."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:190
msgid ""
"It implies that we can always find {math}`s` with {math}`\\operatorname{ulp}"
"(s) = 2^{-2M}`. And from {math}`\\text{(U1)}`, {math}`u = s(1 + m_x) + m_x`, "
"its {math}`ulp` is:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:193
msgid ""
"\\operatorname{ulp}(u) &= \\operatorname{ulp}(s) \\cdot \\operatorname{ulp}"
"(m_x) \\\\\n"
"                      &= 2^{-2M} \\operatorname{ulp}(m_x)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:198 ../../../headers/math/log.md:297
msgid "Since:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:200
msgid "|u| < C = 2^{-N} = 2^{-M - 1},"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:204 ../../../headers/math/log.md:303
msgid "Its required precision is:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:206
msgid ""
"\\operatorname{prec}(u) &= \\log_2(2^{-M-1} / \\operatorname{ulp}(u)) \\\\\n"
"                       &= \\log_2(2^{M - 1} / \\operatorname{ulp}(m_x)) \\"
"\\\n"
"                       &= M - 1 - \\log_2(\\operatorname{ulp}(m_x))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:212
msgid ""
"This means that in this case, we cannot restrict {math}`u` to be exactly "
"representable in double precision for double precision input {math}`x` with "
"{math}`M > 2`. Nonetheless, for a reasonable value of {math}`M`, we can have "
"{math}`u` exactly representable in double precision for single precision "
"input {math}`x` ({math}`\\operatorname{ulp}(m_x) = 2^{-23}`) such that {math}"
"`|u| < 2^{-M - 1}` using a look-up table of size {math}`2^M`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:218
msgid ""
"A particular formula for {math}`s` can be derived from {math}`\\text{(S2')}` "
"by the midpoint formula:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:221
msgid ""
"s &= 2^{-2M} \\operatorname{round}\\left( 2^{2M} \\cdot "
"\\operatorname{midpoint}\n"
"     \\left(-\\frac{-2^{-M - 1} - k2^{-M}}{1 + k 2^{-M}},\n"
"     \\frac{2^{-M-1} - (k + 1)2^{-M}}{1 + (k + 1) 2^{-M}}\\right) \\right) \\"
"\\\n"
"  &= 2^{-2M} \\operatorname{round}\\left( 2^{2M} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} "
"\\left(\n"
"     \\frac{-2^{-M - 1} - k2^{-M}}{1 + k 2^{-M}} +\n"
"     \\frac{2^{-M - 1} + (k + 1)2^{-M}}{1 + (k + 1) 2^{-M}}\n"
"  \\right) \\right) \\\\\n"
"  &= 2^{-2M} \\operatorname{round}\\left( \\frac{\n"
"     - \\left(k + \\frac{1}{2} \\right) \\left(2^M - k - \\frac{1}{2} "
"\\right) }\n"
"     {(1 + k 2^{-N})(1 + (k + 1) 2^{-N})} \\right) \\\\\n"
"  &= - 2^{-2M} \\operatorname{round}\\left( \\frac{\n"
"     \\left(k + \\frac{1}{2} \\right) \\left(2^M - k - \\frac{1}{2} "
"\\right) }\n"
"     {(1 + k 2^{-N})(1 + (k + 1) 2^{-N})} \\right)  \\quad\\quad \\text{(S3)}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:237 ../../../headers/math/log.md:328
msgid "The corresponding range and formula for {math}`r = 1 + s` are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:239
msgid ""
"\\frac{1 - 2^{-M - 1}}{1 + k 2^{-M}} < r \\leq\n"
"\\frac{1 + 2^{-M - 1}}{1 + (k + 1) 2^{-M}}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:244
msgid ""
"r &= 2^{-2M} \\operatorname{round}\\left( 2^{2M} \\cdot\n"
"     \\operatorname{midpoint}\\left( \\frac{1 - 2^{-M - 1}}{1 + k 2^{-M}},\n"
"        \\frac{1 + 2^{-M - 1}}{1 + (k + 1) 2^{-M}}\\right) \\right) \\\\\n"
"  &= 2^{-2M} \\operatorname{round}\\left( 2^{2M} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} "
"\\left(\n"
"     \\frac{1 + 2^{-M-1}}{1 + (k + 1) 2^{-M}} + \\frac{1 - 2^{-M-1}}{1 + k "
"2^{-M}}\n"
"  \\right) \\right) \\\\\n"
"  &= 2^{-2M} \\operatorname{round}\\left( 2^{2M} \\cdot \\frac{\n"
"     1 + \\left(k + \\frac{1}{2} \\right) 2^{-M} - 2^{-2M-2} }{(1 + k 2^{-"
"M})\n"
"     (1 + (k + 1) 2^{-M})} \\right)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:256
msgid "Case 1 - {math}`N = M`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:258
msgid "When {math}`N = M`, {math}`\\text{(S2)}` becomes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:260
msgid ""
"\\frac{-(k + 1)2^{-M}}{1 + k 2^{-M}} < s < \\frac{-k 2^{-M}}{1 + (k + 1) 2^{-"
"M}}\n"
"\\quad\\quad \\text{(S2\")}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:267
msgid ""
"l &= \\frac{- k 2^{-M}}{1 + (k + 1) 2^{-M}} -\n"
"     \\frac{- (k + 1) 2^{-M}}{1 + k 2^{-M}} \\\\\n"
"  &= \\frac{2^{-M} (1 + (2k + 1) 2^{-M})}{(1 + k 2^{-M})(1 + (k + 1)2^{-"
"M})}\n"
"  \\quad\\quad \\text{(L1')}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:274
msgid "As a function of {math}`k`, its derivative with respect to {math}`k`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:276
msgid ""
"\\frac{dl}{dk} =\n"
"-\\frac{2^{-2M}(k(k + 1)2^{-M + 1} + 2^{-M} + 2k + 1)}\n"
"      {(1 + k 2^{-M})^2 (1 + (k + 1) 2^{-M})^2}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:282
msgid ""
"which is always negative for {math}`0 \\leq k \\leq 2^M - 1`. So for {math}"
"`M > 1`, {math}`l` is bounded below by:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:285
msgid "l > \\frac{2^{-M - 1} (3 - 2^{-M})}{2 - 2^{-M}} > 2^{-M - 1}."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:289
msgid ""
"It implies that we can always find {math}`s` with {math}`\\operatorname{ulp}"
"(s) = 2^{-M-1}`. And from {math}`\\text{(U1)}`, {math}`u = s(1 + m_x) + "
"m_x`, its {math}`ulp` is:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:292
msgid ""
"\\operatorname{ulp}(u) &= \\operatorname{ulp}(s) \\cdot \\operatorname{ulp}"
"(m_x) \\\\\n"
"                      &= 2^{-M - 1} \\operatorname{ulp}(m_x)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:299
msgid "|u| < C = 2^{-N} = 2^{-M},"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:305
msgid ""
"\\operatorname{prec}(u) &= \\log_2(2^{-M} / \\operatorname{ulp}(u)) \\\\\n"
"                       &= \\log_2(2 / \\operatorname{ulp}(m_x)) \\\\\n"
"                       &= 1 - \\log_2(\\operatorname{ulp}(m_x))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:311
msgid ""
"Hence, for double precision {math}`x`, {math}`\\operatorname{ulp}(m_x) = "
"2^{-52}`, and the precision needed for {math}`u` is {math}"
"`\\operatorname{prec}(u) = 53`, i.e., {math}`u` can be exactly representable "
"in double precision. And in this case, {math}`s` can be derived from {math}"
"`\\text{(S2\")}` by the midpoint formula:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:316
msgid ""
"s &= 2^{-M - 1} \\operatorname{round}\\left( 2^{M + 1} \\cdot\n"
"     \\operatorname{midpoint} \\left(-\\frac{-(k + 1)2^{-M}}{1 + k 2^{-M}},\n"
"     \\frac{-k2^{-M}}{1 + (k + 1) 2^{-M}}\\right) \\right) \\\\\n"
"  &= 2^{-M - 1} \\operatorname{round}\\left( 2^{M + 1} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} "
"\\left(\n"
"     \\frac{-(k + 1)2^{-M}}{1 + k 2^{-M}} + \\frac{-k2^{-M}}{1 + (k + 1) 2^{-"
"M}}\n"
"     \\right) \\right) \\\\\n"
"  &= -2^{-M - 1} \\operatorname{round}\\left( \\frac{\n"
"     (2k + 1) + (2k^2 + 2k + 1) 2^{-M} }\n"
"     {(1 + k 2^{-N})(1 + (k + 1) 2^{-N})} \\right)  \\quad\\quad "
"\\text{(S3')}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:330
msgid ""
"\\frac{1 - 2^{-M}}{1 + k 2^{-M}} < r \\leq \\frac{1 + 2^{-M}}{1 + (k + 1) "
"2^{-M}}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:334
msgid ""
"r &= 2^{-M-1} \\operatorname{round}\\left( 2^{M + 1} \\cdot\n"
"     \\operatorname{midpoint}\\left( \\frac{1 - 2^{-M}}{1 + k 2^{-M}},\n"
"        \\frac{1 + 2^{-M}}{1 + (k + 1) 2^{-M}}\\right) \\right) \\\\\n"
"  &= 2^{-M-1} \\operatorname{round}\\left( 2^{M + 1} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} "
"\\left(\n"
"     \\frac{1 + 2^{-M}}{1 + (k + 1) 2^{-M}} + \\frac{1 - 2^{-M}}{1 + k 2^{-"
"M}}\n"
"  \\right) \\right) \\\\\n"
"  &= 2^{-M - 1} \\operatorname{round}\\left( 2^{M + 1} \\cdot \\frac{\n"
"     1 + \\left(k + \\frac{1}{2} \\right) 2^{-M} - 2^{-2M-1} }{(1 + k 2^{-"
"M})\n"
"     (1 + (k + 1) 2^{-M})} \\right)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:346
msgid "Edge cases"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:348
msgid "When {math}`k = 0`, notice that:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:350
msgid "0 = k 2^{-N} \\leq m_x < (k + 1) 2^{-N} = 2^{-N} = C,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:354
msgid ""
"so we can simply choose {math}`r = 1` so that {math}`\\log(r) = 0` is exact, "
"then {math}`u = m_x`. This will help reduce the accumulated errors when "
"{math}`m_x` is close to 0 while maintaining the range reduction output's "
"requirements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:358
msgid "When {math}`k = 2^{N} - 1`, {math}`\\text{(S2)}` becomes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:360
msgid ""
"-\\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{C - 2^{-M-1}}{2 - 2^{-M}} <> s \\leq\n"
"-\\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{C}{2}."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:365
msgid "so when {math}`C > 2^{-M - 1}` is a power of 2, we can always choose:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:367
msgid "s = -\\frac{1}{2}, \\quad \\text{i.e.} \\quad r = \\frac{1}{2}."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:371
msgid ""
"This reduction works well to avoid catastrophic cancellation happening when "
"{math}`e_x = -1`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:374
msgid ""
"This also works when {math}`C = 2^{-M - 1}` if we relax the condition on "
"{math}`u` to {math}`|u| \\leq C = 2^{-M-1}`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:377
msgid "Intermediate precision, and Ziv's test"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:379
msgid ""
"In the fast phase, we want extra precision while performant, so we use "
"double-double precision for most intermediate computation steps, and employ "
"Ziv test to see if the result is accurate or not. In our case, the Ziv's "
"test can be described as follow:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:384
msgid ""
"Let {math}`re = re.hi + re.lo` be the double-double output of the fast phase "
"computation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:386
msgid ""
"Let {math}`err` be an estimated upper bound of the errors of {math}`re`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:387
msgid ""
"If {math}`\\circ(re.hi + (re.lo - err)) == \\circ(re.hi + (r.lo + err))` "
"then the result is correctly rounded to double precision for the current "
"rounding mode {math}`\\circ`. Otherwise, the accurate phase with extra "
"precision is needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:391
msgid ""
"For an easy and cheap estimation of the error bound {math}`err`, since the "
"range reduction step described above is accurate, the errors of the result:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:394
msgid ""
"\\log(x) &= e_x \\log(2) - \\log(r) + \\log(1 + u) \\\\\n"
"        &\\approx e_x \\log(2) - \\log(r) + u P(u)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:399
msgid "come from 2 parts:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:401
msgid "the look-up part: {math}`e_x \\log(2) - \\log(r)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:402
msgid "the polynomial approximation part: {math}`u P(u)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:404
msgid ""
"The errors of the first part can be computed with a single {math}"
"`\\operatorname{fma}` operation:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:407
msgid "err_1 = \\operatorname{fma}(e_x, err(\\log(2)), err(\\log(r))),"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:411
msgid ""
"and then combining with the errors of the second part for another {math}"
"`\\operatorname{fma}` operation:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:414
msgid "err = \\operatorname{fma}(u, err(P), err_1)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:418
msgid "Accurate phase"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:420
msgid "Extending range reduction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:422
msgid ""
"Since the output {math}`u = r(1 + m_x) - 1` of the fast phase's range "
"reduction is computed exactly, we can apply further range reduction steps by "
"using the following formula:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:426
msgid "u_{i + 1} = r_i(1 + u_i) - 1 = u_i \\cdot r_i + (r_i - 1),"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:430
msgid ""
"where {math}`|u_i| < 2^{-N_i}` and {math}`u_0 = u` is representable in "
"double precision."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:432
msgid "Let {math}`s_i = r_i - 1`, then we can rewrite it as:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:434
msgid ""
"u_{i + 1} &= (1 + s_i)(1 + u_i) - 1 \\\\\n"
"          &= s_i u_i + u_i + s_i \\\\\n"
"          &= u_i (1 + s_i) + s_i\n"
"          &= s_i (1 + u_i) + u_i."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:441
msgid "Then the bound on {math}`u_{i + 1}` is translated to {math}`s_i` as:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:443
msgid ""
"\\frac{-2^{-N_{i + 1}} - u_i}{1 + u_i} < s_i < \\frac{2^{-N_{i + 1}} - u_i}"
"{1 + u_i}."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:447
msgid ""
"Let say we divide the interval {math}`[0, 2^-{N_i})` into {math}`2^{M_i}` "
"subintervals evenly and use the index {math}`k` such that:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:450
msgid "k 2^{-N_i - M_i} \\leq u_i < (k + 1) 2^{-N_i - M_i},"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:454
msgid ""
"to look-up for the reduction constant {math}`s_{i, k}`. In other word, {math}"
"`k` is given by the formula:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:457
msgid "k = \\left\\lfloor 2^{N_i + M_i} u_i \\right\\rfloor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:461
msgid ""
"Notice that our reduction constant {math}`s_{i, k}` must work for all {math}"
"`u_i` in the interval {math}`I = \\{ v: k 2^{-N_i - M_i} \\leq v < (k + 1) "
"2^{-N_i - M_i} \\}`, so it is bounded by:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:465
msgid ""
"\\sup_{v \\in I} \\frac{-2^{-N_{i + 1}} - v}{1 + v} < s_{i, k} < \\inf_{v "
"\\in I} \\frac{2^{-N_{i + 1}} - v}{1 + v}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:469
msgid ""
"For a fixed constant {math}`|C| < 1`, let {math}`f(v) = \\frac{C - v}{1 + v}"
"`, then its derivative is:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:472
msgid ""
"f'(v) = \\frac{(-1)(1 + v) - (1)(C - v)}{(1 + v)^2} = \\frac{-1 - C}{(1 + "
"v)^2}."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:476
msgid ""
"Since {math}`|C| < 1`, {math}`f'(v) < 0` for all {math}`v \\neq -1`, so:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:478
msgid ""
"\\sup_{v \\in I} f(v) &= f \\left( \\inf\\{ v: v \\in I \\} \\right)\n"
"                     = f \\left( k 2^{-N_i - M_i} \\right) \\\\\n"
"\\inf_{v \\in I} f(v) &= f \\left( \\sup\\{ v: v \\in I \\} \\right)\n"
"                     = f \\left( (k + 1) 2^{-N_i - M_i} \\right)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:485
msgid "Hence we have the following bound on {math}`s_{i, k}`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:487
msgid ""
"\\frac{-2^{-N_{i + 1}} - k 2^{-N_i - M_i}}{1 + k 2^{-N_i - M_i}} < s_{i, k}\n"
"\\leq \\frac{2^{-N_{i + 1}} - (k + 1) 2^{-N_i - M_i}}{1 + (k + 1) 2^{-N_i - "
"M_i}}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:492
msgid "This interval is of length:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:494
msgid ""
"l &= \\frac{2^{-N_{i + 1}} - (k + 1) 2^{-N_i - M_i}}{1 + (k + 1) 2^{-N_i - "
"M_i}} -\n"
"\\frac{-2^{-N_{i + 1}} - k 2^{-N_i - M_i}}{1 + k 2^{-N_i - M_i}} \\\\\n"
"&= \\frac{2^{-N_{i + 1} + 1} - 2^{-N_i - M_i} + (2k + 1) 2^{-N_{i + 1} - N_i "
"- M_i}}\n"
"    {(1 + k 2^{-N_i - M_i})(1 + (k + 1) 2^{-N_i -M_i})}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:501
msgid "So in order to be able to find {math}`s_{i, k}`, we need that:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:503
msgid ""
"2^{-N_{i + 1} + 1} - 2^{-N_i - M_i} + (2k + 1) 2^{-N_{i + 1} - N_i - M_i} > 0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:507
msgid "This give us the following bound on {math}`N_{i + 1}`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:509
msgid "N_{i + 1} \\leq N_i + M_i + 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:513
msgid ""
"To make the range reduction effective, we will want to maximize {math}`N_{i "
"+ 1}`, so let consider the two cases: {math}`N_{i + 1} = N_i + M_i + 1` and "
"{math}`N_{i + 1} = N_i + M_i`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:517
msgid ""
"The optimal choice to balance between maximizing {math}`N_{i + 1}` and "
"minimizing the precision needed for {math}`s_{i, k}` is:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:520
msgid "N_{i + 1} = N_i + M_i,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:524
msgid "and in this case, the optimal {math}`\\operatorname{ulp}(s_{i, k})` is:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:526
msgid "\\operatorname{ulp}(s_{i, k}) = 2^{-N_i - M_i}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:530
msgid "and the corresponding {math}`\\operatorname{ulp}(u_{i + 1})` is:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:532
msgid ""
"\\operatorname{ulp}(u_{i + 1}) &= \\operatorname{ulp}(u_i) "
"\\operatorname{ulp}(s_{i, k}) \\\\\n"
"  &= \\operatorname{ulp}(u_i) \\cdot 2^{-N_i - M_i} \\\\\n"
"  &= \\operatorname{ulp}(u_0) \\cdot 2^{-N_0 - M_0} \\cdot 2^{-N_0 - M_0 - "
"M_1} \\cdots 2^{-N_0 - M_0 - M_1 - \\cdots - M_i} \\\\\n"
"  &= 2^{-N_0 - 53} \\cdot 2^{-N_0 - M_0} \\cdot 2^{-N_0 - M_0 - M_1} \\cdots "
"2^{-N_0 - M_0 - M_1 - \\cdots - M_i}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:539
msgid ""
"Since {math}`|u_{i + 1}| < 2^{-N_{i + 1}} = 2^{-N_0 - M_1 - ... -M_i}`, the "
"precision of {math}`u_{i + 1}` is:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:542
msgid ""
"\\operatorname{prec}(u_{i + 1}) &= (N_0 + 53) + (N_0 + M_0) + \\cdots +\n"
"  (N_0 + M_0 + \\cdots + M_i) - (N_0 + M_0 + \\cdots + M_i) \\\\\n"
"  &= (i + 1) N_0 + i M_0 + (i - 1) M_1 + \\cdots + M_{i - 1} + 53"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:548
msgid ""
"If we choose to have the same {math}`M_0 = M_1 = \\cdots = M_i = M`, this "
"can be simplified to:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/log.md:551
msgid ""
"\\operatorname{prec}(u_{i + 1}) = (i + 1) N_0 + \\frac{i(i + 1)}{2} \\cdot M "
"+ 53."
msgstr ""

